    {
      "type": "callout",
      "tone": "info",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Four chords everybody plays in the first three frets, and four different forms — and the "
        },
        {
          "text": "F",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", barred at fret 1, is the only one of them that is not an open shape."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Nobody ever points that out, and it is why the "
        },
        {
          "text": "F",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " always felt like the odd one out among four supposedly equal beginner chords: it is the only barre in the set."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Each of those four chords has five forms, not one, so this loop isn't really four places on the neck — it's twenty, and open position is just the one you were shown first. Every window, recomputed:"
