    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The "
        },
        {
          "text": "i",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " is the one that moves — two frets further up than the other three settle. The reason is "
        },
        {
          "text": "the same one chapter 2 found",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "minor-caged-triad-g-form"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ": the G form of a minor chord can't be barred, so "
        },
        {
          "text": "Am",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "'s window at "
        },
        {
          "text": "1–5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " isn't an option, and the E form's barre at fret "
        },
        {
          "text": "5",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " is the nearest thing standing in for it."
        }
      ]
